# A store whose value reads the buffer it writes. The value is read whole, before the store:
# x = [1 2 3 4]; x[1..3] = old x[0..2] = [1 2 3], so x becomes [1 1 2 3], not [1 1 1 1].
%x    = buffer 4 slot=0 dtype=i32
%sx   = store %x [1 2 3 4]
%x1   = after %x %sx
%s    = store (shrink %x1 1 3) (load (shrink %x1 0 3))
%test = assert (after %x %s) [1 1 2 3]
